<item><title>IMF approves $425 million programme for Guinea, leaves subsidy cuts to government</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/gn/imf-approves-425-million-programme-for-guinea-leaves-6ea0ab/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/gn/imf-approves-425-million-programme-for-guinea-leaves-6ea0ab/</guid><category>Guinea</category><description>The 2026-2029 deal calls for a strategy to reduce subsidies, while Guinea decides when to act and strengthens support for vulnerable households.</description><pubDate>Sat, 28 Nov 2026 09:09:08 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/gn/imf-approves-425-million-programme-for-guinea-leaves-6ea0ab/share.jpg" length="44753" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/gn/imf-approves-425-million-programme-for-guinea-leaves-6ea0ab/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
